# Release owners (BloxBean release-ops standard). Combined with the `protected-branches` ruleset's "Require review
# from Code Owners" on main, a PR that touches any of these paths needs an approving review from one of them.
# Changing `version` in package.json releases the site (after approval in the `release` environment), and the
# other paths decide what the release builds and how it is published.
#
# There is intentionally no catch-all `*` rule: other paths stay unowned and need only the usual review.
# CODEOWNERS is last-match-wins, so keep these patterns non-overlapping.
#
# For now the release owner is @satran004 (also the `release` environment reviewer). Later, replace it with the
# org team @bloxbean/release-owners (the release-ops standard), give the team write access, and make it the
# reviewer of the `release` and `github-pages` environments.

# This file, so the protection can't be removed without a release owner.
/.github/CODEOWNERS      @satran004

# Workflows: what runs, and what gets published.
/.github/workflows/      @satran004

# Version bump -> release. Dependencies are bundled into the published site.
/package.json            @satran004
/package-lock.json       @satran004

# Build configuration of the published site.
/svelte.config.js        @satran004
/vite.config.ts          @satran004
